Registered acquisition includes a two-storey house numbered 12/1 (specifically listed as two bedrooms and three bathrooms); a single-storey semi-detached residence numbered 12; a single-storey semi-detached residence numbered 10 with concrete fence; and an unnumbered single-storey house with garage. The aggregate six-bedroom/six-bathroom count is retained from SAM''s summary; the 12/1 counts are not added again. Verify each structure and the transfer schedule.

Polygonal land with approximately 44.5 metres of northern frontage and maximum depth 26 metres. SAM reports red zoning and residential surroundings.

Material access issue: SAM describes Prem Chai Rat Soi 3 as public, with approximately four metres of concrete carriageway and seven metres right of way. However, property access passes through front road title 191390, parcel 218. SAM reports that this parcel has not been dedicated as public land according to its title, although it is a concrete road maintained by Saen Suk Municipality. Verify road status, evidence of access rights over 191390, boundaries and actual use before offering. Municipal maintenance does not confirm public ownership of the road parcel.

Nearby source-listed places are Bang Sai Police Station, Nong Mon Market, Wat Tan Lom and Wat Rat Sattha School. From Chon Buri toward Pattaya on Sukhumvit, pass Wat Chaeng Charoen Don and Sukhum Witthaya School, turn left onto Highway 3144, right into Prem Chai Rat Road for 1.2 kilometres, then left into Soi 3 for 106 metres; the property is on the right.

Building/interior photos display 22 February 2025. Twenty-one images include homes, halls, rooms, stairs, bathrooms, garage, plot/building plans and map. Inspect each building''s current structure, roof, power, plumbing and drainage.

